<title>SINGAPORE: Lung Kee Metal jumps 63 pct at debut.</title>
<headline>Lung Kee Metal jumps 63 pct at debut.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Singapore's Lung Kee Metal Holdings Ltd jumped 63 percent from their initial public offer price of US$0.55 to a high of US$0.90 on their first morning of trading on Thursday.  </p>
<p>More than 15 million shares in the company changed hands in the first 20 minutes of trading. The stock had settled back to around US$0.855 by 0120 GMT.</p>
<p>Lung Kee Metal, which makes mould bases and trades in metals, industry oil and machinery, said on Wednesday the public portion of its share offer was approximately 28 times subscribed.</p>
<p>It had offered 50 million shares, 40 via private placement and the rest to the public.</p>
<p>The company is also listed in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
